      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_Green%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The current name of Fountain Green comes from the springs and green pastures near the original town site.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_Green%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office called Fountain Green has been in operation since 1860.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain_Green%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Fountain Green Woolgrowers Association was founded in 1908 and became a dominant group in town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
